			"notes": "## Holoscreen 0.1.0\n\nHoloscreen now runs on many more Minecraft versions. Each version has its own jar: download the one that matches your game.\n\n| Minecraft | File |\n|---|---|\n| 1.21.1 | `holoscreen-0.1.0+mc1.21.1.jar` |\n| 1.21.2 – 1.21.3 | `holoscreen-0.1.0+mc1.21.2-1.21.3.jar` |\n| 1.21.4 | `holoscreen-0.1.0+mc1.21.4.jar` |\n| 1.21.10 | `holoscreen-0.1.0+mc1.21.10.jar` |\n| 1.21.11 | `holoscreen-0.1.0+mc1.21.11.jar` |\n| 26.1 – 26.1.2 | `holoscreen-0.1.0+mc26.1.x.jar` |\n| 26.2 | `holoscreen-0.1.0+mc26.2.x.jar` |\n| 26.3 | `holoscreen-0.1.0+mc26.3.x.jar` |\n\n1.21.5 – 1.21.9 are not supported, because no Chromium library exists for those versions.\n\n### What's new\n- Support for Minecraft 1.21.2 – 1.21.4, 1.21.10, 1.21.11 and 26.1 – 26.3, on top of 1.21.1.\n- From 1.21.10 on, the browser runs on [MCEF Modern](https://github.com/DimasKama/mcef-modern), which is bundled like MCEF.\n- If Chromium is still starting when you place a screen, a chat message tells you, and the screen appears as soon as Chromium is ready.\n\n### Install\nYou need Fabric Loader and Fabric API for your version. Drop the jar in your `mods` folder. The browser library is bundled. The first time you open a screen, Chromium is downloaded (about 100 MB).\n\nPublic screens need Holoscreen on the server too. Dedicated servers no longer need MCEF installed.\n\n### Known issues\n- Some Twitch and Kick streams might not play, because the Chromium build doesn't ship every video codec.\n- With an Iris shader pack on, the screen is always drawn on top of the world.\n- On 26.3, the \"over blocks\" mode also draws over players and mobs standing in front of the screen.\n\n### Credits\nThe browser comes from [MCEF](https://github.com/CinemaMod/mcef) by CinemaMod (up to 1.21.4) and [MCEF Modern](https://github.com/DimasKama/mcef-modern) by DimasKama (1.21.10 and later). Both are included unmodified under LGPL-2.1. Holoscreen itself is MIT licensed."
